-- title:
--   Representations of the infinite cyclic group reduce to measure equivalence
-- statement:
--   Let $H=\ell^2(\mathbb N,\mathbb C)$, and let $\operatorname{Rep}(\mathbb Z,H)$ be the space of all unitary representations of the infinite cyclic group on $H$, equipped with the Borel structure generated by strong pointwise evaluation. Write $\rho\cong\sigma$ when one unitary on $H$ intertwines every represented group element. There is a Borel map $\rho\mapsto\mu_\rho$ to the probability measures on Cantor space such that
--
--   $$\rho\cong\sigma\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\mu_\rho\ll\mu_\sigma\ \text{and}\ \mu_\sigma\ll\mu_\rho.$$
--
--   The statement concerns all representations of the cyclic group; it imposes no cyclic-vector hypothesis. It is the reverse comparison in the first part of Theorem 1.6 of Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.6; source BenchmarkOperatorTransport.lean, lines 135–140; source SHA-256 114aff4f6643ef17fa6a0383fa890dcea4b125ca5a8e4ff0e94b7ab7242aa0b3. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (source commit not yet published).

